chat_memory.prompt:
A talk between {name} and {player}:
{talk}
Write, as {name}'s own short note to self, what {name} will remember of it: what {player} wanted, offered or said, any price or promise named, how it went, and what {name} thinks of {player} now. Two or three short sentences, in the third person about {player}, keeping every name, car and figure as said. The note only: no heading, no 'Note to self'.

chat_summary.prompt:
{name} and {player} are talking.
What was said before, in short: {earlier}
Then:
{talk}
Sum up everything said so far, the short version above and the lines after it, as notes for {name} to carry on the talk: what {player} wants, every price, offer and promise named and who named it ({name} asking, {player} offering), what was agreed or turned down, and the mood. At most four short sentences, in the third person, keeping every name, car and figure exactly as said and adding none. The notes only: no heading.
